<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">1. Executive Summary &amp; Problem Space</h2>

High-density enterprise tech hubs and global delivery centers such as <strong>[24]7.ai</strong> circulate thousands of IT hardware assets—including Dell OptiPlex desktop workstations, dual-screen monitor setups, rack servers, developer laptops, and high-performance network switches. These computing resources continuously transit across warehouse stockrooms, staging areas, executive rooms, and dedicated production floors (e.g., Floor 2, Floor 3, and Floor 7).

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">The Critical Vulnerabilities of Legacy Tracking</h3>
Traditional paper passes, spreadsheet registers, or disconnected ticketing queues introduce severe governance and physical security risks:
1. <strong>The "Ghost Asset" Vulnerability:</strong> Equipment moves physically across doors and floors without real-time perimeter validation.
2. <strong>Serial Number Swapping &amp; Hardware Substitution:</strong> Faulty or unapproved hardware substituted for production-certified machines during transit.
3. <strong>Decommission Leakage:</strong> Scrapped or End-of-Life (EOL) hardware inadvertently placed back into active circulation.
4. <strong>Network Topology Mismatch:</strong> Workstations moved without updating switch port assignments (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">P-204</code>, <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">SW03-P24</code>), causing broadcast storms and unmapped IP leases.

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">The Architectural Solution</h3>
The <strong>[24]7.ai Asset Tracking Platform</strong> enforces an automated, zero-trust chain of custody:
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>No movement occurs without a digital ticket</strong> containing origin, destination, designated custodian, reason, and switch port allocation.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Separation of Duties (SoD):</strong> Engineers request movements; designated Approval Managers (Jyothi Potula / D. Manoharan) digitally sign off; Gate Security Officers verify physical hardware at the perimeter.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Sub-millisecond dual-mode barcode/QR verification</strong> at Platina Security Gate.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Permanent, tamper-evident audit trail</strong> logging every scan, approval, and custody transition.</li>

---

<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">2. Global System Architecture</h2>

The application is architected around a high-performance <strong>Single-Binary Node.js / Express 4.21 Engine</strong> serving an optimized, statically compiled <strong>React 19 Single Page Application (SPA)</strong> behind an <strong>Nginx Layer-7 Reverse Proxy with SSL/TLS Termination</strong>.

