<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3. Frontend Architecture &amp; Role-Based UI Modules</h2>

The frontend is built with <strong>React 19</strong> using <strong>TypeScript</strong> for end-to-end type safety, compiled via <strong>Vite 6</strong> into an ultra-lean static distribution styled with modern <strong>Tailwind CSS</strong>.

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">
                                  [24]7.ai Asset Tracking Portal
                                                 │
          ┌──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┐
          │                                      │                                      │
          ▼                                      ▼                                      ▼
      MODULE A                                MODULE B                               MODULE C
IT Field Engineer Desk                 Approval Manager Desk                  Platina Gate Security
───────────────────────                ──────────────────────                 ──────────────────────
• Ticket Generation                    • 1-Click Ticket Approval              • USB Laser Barcode Gun Scan
• 7th Floor Visual Map                 • 1-Click Ticket Rejection             • HTML5 Camera Stream Engine
• Port Allocation (P-204)              • Scrap/Custody Backtracking           • Real-time Green/Red Clearance
• Asset S/N Normalization              • Master CSV / Excel Audit Export      • Security Gate Audit Trail
• Direct Stock Re-indexing             • Executive AI Chatbot Hub             • Anti-Tamper Serial Trap
</pre>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3.1 Module A: IT Field Engineer Desk (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">MovementDesk.tsx</code>, <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">FloorMap7th.tsx</code>)</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Role Objective:</strong> Field operations interface for raising movement tickets and mapping physical hardware layout.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Component Capabilities:</strong></li>
  * <strong>Interactive 7th Floor Visual Map:</strong> A graphical grid mapping work bays to physical network switch ports (e.g., Switch 03, Port 24, Bay P-204). Engineers select the exact bay to automatically populate network port documentation.
  * <strong>Ticket Genesis Engine:</strong> Creates standardized movement orders (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">TKT-0001</code>, <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">TKT-0002</code>) with validated serial tags, origin location (Stock, Bay), destination, and engineering justification.
  * <strong>Barcode Input Sanitization:</strong> Automatically cleans serial strings pasted or scanned by engineers, removing trailing hardware prefixes or whitespaces.
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Separation of Duties (SoD) Rule:</strong> Field Engineers <strong>cannot approve their own tickets</strong> and <strong>cannot trigger gate clearance</strong>.</li>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3.2 Module B: Approval Manager Desk (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">ApprovalManagerDesk.tsx</code>, <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">AdminReportingView.tsx</code>)</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Role Objective:</strong> Authoritative governance, executive audit, and sign-off hub restricted to designated managers (Jyothi Potula / D. Manoharan).</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Component Capabilities:</strong></li>
  * <strong>Real-time Pending Approval Queue:</strong> Reviews movements with full visibility of origin, target floor, requesting engineer, and justification before approving or rejecting with remarks.
  * <strong>Reversible Custody &amp; Scrap Decommission Terminal:</strong> Ability to reverse asset movements back into IT stock or formally decommission units into the scrap pool with permanent state locking.
  * <strong>Executive AI Chatbot Assistant (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">ChatbotAssistant.tsx</code>):</strong> Natural-language querying interface integrated directly with the asset inventory database for fast stock inquiries.
  * <strong>Master Compliance Export Center:</strong> One-click export of unified audit records into CSV and Excel formats, plus the downloadable technical architecture document.

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3.3 Module C: Platina Gate Security Terminal (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">ScannerGate.tsx</code>, <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">HardwareBarcodeScanner.tsx</code>)</h3>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Role Objective:</strong> Physical security perimeter checkpoint operated by security gate guards.</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:4pt;"><strong>Component Capabilities:</strong></li>
  * <strong>Dual-Mode Barcode Scanning:</strong>
    * <strong>Optical Camera Scanning:</strong> Integrated HTML5 30 FPS camera feed decoding Code-128, Code-39, and QR codes.
    * <strong>USB Laser Gun Barcode Scanning:</strong> Direct capture of physical handheld laser scanners (Honeywell, Zebra, Symbol) sending keystrokes in Human Interface Device (HID) keyboard emulation mode.
  * <strong>Sub-Millisecond Clearance Decision:</strong> Evaluates scanned serial against approved tickets in under 5 ms:
    * <strong>GREEN PASS:</strong> Displays approved ticket number, asset details, destination floor, and updates custody state to <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">CLEARED</code>.
    * <strong>RED SECURITY ALERT:</strong> Triggers high-visibility audio/visual lockdown if an unapproved, expired, or unregistered serial tag is scanned, logging an unauthorized transit attempt into audit logs.

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">3.4 Hardware Barcode Normalization Engine (<code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">serialValidator.ts</code>)</h3>
<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">typescript
/<em></em>
 * Normalizes input from optical camera readers and physical USB laser guns.
 * Strips hardware vendor prefixes, non-printable characters, and whitespace.
 */
export function sanitizeSerialNumber(rawInput: string): string {
  if (!rawInput) return '';
  return rawInput
    .trim()
    .toUpperCase()
    .replace(/^(S\/N|SN|SERIAL|TAG|ASSET)[:\-_\s]*/i, '') // Strips vendor prefixes
    .replace(/[\x00-\x1F\x7F]/g, '');                   // Strips ASCII control bytes
}
</pre>

