<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">5. Nginx Reverse Proxy Architecture &amp; SSL/TLS Termination</h2>

In corporate enterprise infrastructure, client workstations across different subnets cannot connect directly to application runtime ports due to network isolation. Nginx serves as the primary ingress controller on Rocky Linux 9.

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
<table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:16px 0; font-size:10pt; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">
  <tr style="background-color:#0f3b7a; color:#ffffff;">
    <th style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px; text-align:left;">NGINX INGRESS CONFIGURATION</th>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">[ Client: TCP 80 (HTTP) ]   ──► HTTP 301 Redirect ──► [ Client: TCP 443 ]</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">[ Client: TCP 443 (HTTPS) ] ──► SSL Termination   ──► [ Upstream Proxy ]</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">(TLS 1.2 / TLS 1.3)   Passes to 127.0.0.1:3000</td>
  </tr>
</table>

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
</pre>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">5.1 Production Nginx Virtual Host Configuration</h3>
File path: <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">/etc/nginx/conf.d/asset-tracker.conf</code>

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">nginx
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">==============================================================================</h1>
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">[24]7.ai Asset Tracker - Production Nginx Reverse Proxy Configuration</h1>
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">==============================================================================</h1>

<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">1. Plain HTTP (Port 80) -&gt; Force Redirect to HTTPS (Port 443)</h1>
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name _;

    # Immediate 301 Permanent Redirect
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}

<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">2. Secure HTTPS (Port 443) -&gt; Reverse Proxy to Node.js (Port 3000)</h1>
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name _;

    # SSL Certificate Paths (Enterprise Wildcard or Local RSA)
    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/asset-tracker.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/asset-tracker.key;

    # SSL Protocols &amp; Modern Ciphers
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
    ssl_ciphers ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384;
    ssl_prefer_server_ciphers on;
    ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:10m;
    ssl_session_timeout 1d;
    ssl_session_tickets off;

    # Enterprise Security Headers
    add_header X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;
    add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;
    add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains" always;

    # Maximum payload size for audit exports and batch inventory syncs
    client_max_body_size 50M;

    # Reverse Proxy Location Routing
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;

        # WebSocket &amp; Upstream Connection Headers
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        
        # Real IP &amp; Forwarded Headers for Audit Logging
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;

        # Proxy Timeout Safeguards
        proxy_connect_timeout 60s;
        proxy_send_timeout 60s;
        proxy_read_timeout 60s;
        proxy_buffering off;
    }

    # Static Asset Caching Policy
    location ~* \.(js|css|png|jpg|jpeg|gif|ico|svg|woff|woff2|doc)$ {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        expires 30d;
        add_header Cache-Control "public, no-transform";
    }
}
</pre>

<h3 style="color:#1e293b; margin-top: 18px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">5.2 SELinux &amp; Rocky Linux Firewall Hardening</h3>
<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">bash
<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">1. Allow Nginx reverse proxy connections through SELinux</h1>
setsebool -P httpd_can_network_connect 1

<h1 style="color:#0f3b7a; border-bottom: 2px solid #0f3b7a; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 28px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">2. Allow HTTPS and HTTP services permanently in firewalld</h1>
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-service=https
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-service=http
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-port=443/tcp
firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-port=80/tcp
firewall-cmd --reload
</pre>

