<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">6. End-to-End Asset Movement Lifecycle &amp; Data Flow</h2>

<pre style="background-color:#f8fafc; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:12px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:9.5pt; border-radius:4px; line-height:1.4;">
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
<table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:16px 0; font-size:10pt; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">
  <tr style="background-color:#0f3b7a; color:#ffffff;">
    <th style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px; text-align:left;">AUDIT-COMPLIANT DATA FLOW PIPELINE</th>
  </tr>
</table>

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

  STEP 1: INITIATION (Field Engineer Desk)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Engineer selects Asset [Dell OptiPlex 7090 | S/N-78F8A2]
  Input: Destination = Floor 7, Bay 14 | Switch Port = P-204 | Justification = Production Refresh
  Action: POST /api/movement/tickets
  State: TICKET_CREATED | Status: PENDING_APPROVAL
  Audit Record: [Timestamp: T0, User: engineer@247.ai, Action: CREATE_TICKET, Hash: H1]
       │
       ▼
  STEP 2: GOVERNANCE SIGN-OFF (Approval Manager Desk)
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Manager reviews justification, physical location, and engineer identity
  Action: POST /api/movement/tickets/TKT-0001/approve
  State: TICKET_APPROVED | Status: APPROVED
  Audit Record: [Timestamp: T1, Approver: jyothi.potula@247.ai, Action: APPROVE_TICKET, Hash: H2]
       │
       ▼
  STEP 3: PHYSICAL TRANSIT &amp; GATE CLEARANCE (Platina Gate Clearance)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Guard scans hardware barcode at physical gate using USB Laser Gun / Camera
  Action: POST /api/gate/verify
  Verification:
    ├── Does Scanned Serial == Approved Ticket Serial? (YES)
    └── Is Ticket Status == APPROVED? (YES)
  State: GATE_CLEARED | Status: CLEARED
  Audit Record: [Timestamp: T2, Guard: guard.platina@247.ai, Action: GATE_SCAN_PASS, Hash: H3]
       │
       ▼
  STEP 4: PHYSICAL BAY DEPLOYMENT (Floor 7 Bay 14)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Hardware connected to Network Switch Port P-204
  State: ASSET_DEPLOYED | Location: FLOOR 7 | Switch Port: P-204
  Audit Record: [Timestamp: T3, System: AUTO_INDEXER, Action: ASSET_DEPLOYED, Hash: H4]
       │
       ▼
  STEP 5: REVERSE CUSTODY / DECOMMISSION (Scrap / Return to Stock)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  If hardware is decommissioned or designated for EOL disposal:
  Action: POST /api/backtrack
  Choices:
    ├── RETURN_TO_STOCK: Re-indexes to IT Stock Room inventory
    └── BACK_TO_SCRAP: Permanently locks asset from future deployments
  Audit Record: [Timestamp: T4, User: manager@247.ai, Action: DECOMMISSION_SCRAP, Hash: H5]
</pre>

---

<h2 style="color:#1e40af; border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 24px; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">7. Audit Compliance Verification Matrix (ISO 27001 &amp; SOC 2)</h2>

<table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:16px 0; font-size:10pt; font-family:Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;">
  <tr style="background-color:#0f3b7a; color:#ffffff;">
    <th style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px; text-align:left;">Regulatory Standard</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px; text-align:left;">Compliance Control Description</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px; text-align:left;">Platform Implementation Mechanism</th>
    <th style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px; text-align:left;">Audit Evidence Artifact</th>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"><strong>ISO/IEC 27001 A.8.1</strong></td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Inventory of Assets</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Centralized registry containing hardware serials, MAC addresses, models, and locations.</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"><code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">/api/assets</code>, Master CSV Export</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"><strong>ISO/IEC 27001 A.8.2</strong></td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Ownership &amp; Custodianship</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Every asset maintains an unambiguous custodian (Engineer, Manager, or Guard) at all times.</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Record field: <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">currentCustodian</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"><strong>ISO/IEC 27001 A.11.2</strong></td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Physical Equipment Transit</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Perimeter clearance terminal blocks any unauthorized hardware removal.</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Security Terminal: <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">ScannerGate.tsx</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"><strong>SOC 2 Type II CC6.1</strong></td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Logical Access &amp; SoD</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Role-based segregation: Engineers cannot approve their own tickets.</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Middleware: <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">verifyRole()</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"><strong>SOC 2 Type II CC6.8</strong></td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Tamper-Evident Audit Logging</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Immutable audit log capturing timestamp, actor ID, and IP address for all operations.</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Store: <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">database.json</code>, Systemd logs</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background-color:#ffffff;">
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;"><strong>SOC 2 Type II CC7.2</strong></td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Security Anomaly Detection</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Scans of unapproved or invalid barcodes trigger logged security alerts.</td>
    <td style="border:1px solid #cbd5e1; padding:8px;">Event: <code style="background-color:#f1f5f9; padding:2px 4px; font-family:Consolas, Courier New, monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">SECURITY_BREACH_ALERT</code></td>
  </tr>
</table>


